{"reply": "Hi Henry, I'm sorry about the stress. I can't tell the shop it's a defect. That's for the technician's finding and the warranty desk to decide. If you disagree with the finding, I can ask a person to arrange a documented second inspection.

Your warranty facts: basic (3 years / 60,000 km), powertrain (5 years / 100,000 km) and corrosion (7 years) are all still within their limits. Basic coverage excludes damage from accidents. Whether this water damage is covered can only be decided by the warranty desk after an inspection, so I can't say yes or no.

I'm passing your file to a colleague now, so they can follow up with you about the second inspection.", "action": "escalated", "escalation_reason": "policy_limit", "summary": "Customer Lee (verified via RO-663631) was told by the shop that water damage came from a flood in an underground parking garage. The customer believes it is a car leak and asked us to label it a defect to avoid an insurance deductible. I did not do that and did not open a claim (P-09). I gave the warranty facts: basic, powertrain and corrosion are all within limits, and the warranty desk decides. Please arrange a documented second inspection if the customer still disputes the finding.", "policy_rules_cited": ["P-01", "P-03", "P-04", "P-09", "P-08"]}
